# Always commit and push

When you finish implementing or modifying code in this repo:

1. Commit the relevant changes with a concise message (follow the repo's git safety protocol).
2. Push to the tracked remote branch immediately (`git push` / `git push -u origin HEAD` as needed).
3. Do this without waiting for the user to ask again — treat "push when done" as standing policy for this project.

Exceptions: do not commit secrets (`.env`, credentials). Do not force-push to main/master unless the user explicitly requests it.
